                <pb facs="0747" n="613" sameAs="frus:frus1888p1/pg613"/>

                <head>No. 445.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Pendleton to Mr. Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-02-20"><hi rendition="#italic">February</hi> 20, 1888</date>.
                        (Received March 8.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 583.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my dispatch No. 574, of the
                    30th ultimo, with which I inclosed a bill amending the “socialist law,” then
                    pending before the Reichstag, I have now the honor to inform you that the
                    validity of the original law has been prolonged for a period of two years, to
                    expire September 30, 1890, the Reichstag declining to adopt any of the
                    amendments proposed by the Government.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Geo. H.
                    Pendleton.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
